**Lemma 5.3 (actual matched-coordinate converse).** Let $A,B$ be finite occurrence families and $s:C\hookrightarrow A$, $t:C\hookrightarrow B$ two embeddings. For $\epsilon\ge0$, assume on every matched occurrence $c$ that

$$b_{t(c)}\le b_{s(c)}+\epsilon,\qquad b_{s(c)}\le b_{t(c)}+\epsilon,$$

and

$$d_{t(c)}\le T_\epsilon(d_{s(c)}),\qquad d_{s(c)}\le T_\epsilon(d_{t(c)}),$$

where $T_\epsilon(d)=d+\epsilon$ for finite $d$ and $T_\epsilon(\infty)=\infty$. Assume every unmatched occurrence $a$ or $b$ has death at most its birth plus $2\epsilon$. Then the actual supported interval sums admit natural maps $I_A\to I_B(\epsilon)$ and $I_B\to I_A(\epsilon)$ with both shifted composites equal to their actual $2\epsilon$ structure maps. These extended death inequalities are exactly finite death deviations at most $\epsilon$ and essential-to-essential pairing; unmatched essentials are excluded by the length inequality.

